title: The vine and the locket
story: fernhill
continues: machine
description: Warmth in the pipes moved the vine to flowering from a room away.
  Pruning it is how Verity's locket comes out of the ground.

---

> west
[OK: contains "Fountain Court"]

> north
[OK: contains "Entrance Hall"]

> east
[OK: contains "Kitchen"]

> take the garden shears
[OK: contains "Taken"]
[STATE: true, player.inventory contains shears]

> west
[OK: contains "Entrance Hall"]

# Leaving the House for the Grounds fires `cold-returns`, and this is its
# first-time variant — the player has not been out and back before.
> south
[OK: contains "The cold finds you the moment you step out, and means it"]

> west
[OK: contains "Greenhouse"]

# KNOWN STORY BUG, asserted as it behaves. The boiler moved the vine to
# `flowering` (machine.transcript, terminal state `on enter`), but the vine's
# description is static prose and still says seedling. The next command acts on
# `flowering`, so the description and the state disagree in front of the player.
> examine the vine
[OK: contains "barely more than a seedling now"]

# `when flowering` — three clean cuts, and the locket is moved into the room.
> prune the vine
[OK: contains "a single heavy fruit swells, splits"]
[OK: contains "something small and silver slides out into the leaf mould"]
[STATE: true, locket.location = Greenhouse]

> take the silver locket
[OK: contains "Taken"]
[STATE: true, player.inventory contains locket]

# `when fruiting` — the third branch, and the vine is done.
> prune the vine
[OK: contains "The vine has given everything it kept"]

# The same north door frost-seal.transcript could not open. Warmth shifted it.
> north
[OK: contains "Folly Hill"]
[OK: contains "on its crown stands the folly"]
[STATE: true, player.location = Folly Hill]

# lit (10) + fruited (5).
> score
[OK: contains "You have scored 15 out of 50"]
